      ":question/id": "7d9e7c1e-feab-55c0-a7c7-e8a9b05fd45b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + y^{2} \\cos^{2}{(5 x )}=(- y \\cos{(5 x )} + 5)^{2}\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + y^{2} \\cos^{2}{(5 x )}&=(- y \\cos{(5 x )} + 5)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + y^{2} \\cos^{2}{(5 x )}&=y^{2} \\cos^{2}{(5 x )} - 10 y \\cos{(5 x )} + 25 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=- 10 y \\cos{(5 x )} + 25 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(10 \\cos{(5 x )})}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{25}_{Q(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=10 \\cos{(5 x )}$ and $Q(x)=25.$",
